ads the base’s rows, shifted where they hold hyperedges:","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"successorIndices(ofIndex: i)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is ","type":"text"},{"code":"outHyperedgeIndices(ofIndex: i)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" plus n, and of ","type":"text"},{"code":"n + p","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" it is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"targetIndices(ofHyperedgeAt: p)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"; ","type":"text"},{"code":"predecessorIndices","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is ","type":"text"},{"code":"inHyperedgeIndices","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" plus n, or","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"sourceIndices","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". Graph algorithms therefore run on the view without hashing a vertex. The view","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"does not offer ","type":"text"},{"code":"_withSuccessorIndexRows","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", whose contract needs edge positions in row order.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Costs are as for ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"IncidenceGraphView"},{"text":": O(1) reads on ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"IncidenceList"},{"text":", which stores its","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"incidences; on another base a hyperedge’s incidence numbers are a range, O(1), ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"edges[q]"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"binary-searches and selects by rank, O(log m + ⌈n\/64⌉) on ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"OrientedIncidenceMatrix"},{"text":", and a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"vertex’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"outEdges"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"inEdges"},{"text":" is computed from ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_memberRank"},{"text":", O(d·⌈n\/64⌉) on","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code"